## dashboard-fsrs run summary

The Must-have dashboard is built: one SQL read per request, the `GET /api/dashboard` route, the privacy tests, and the Svelte screen. T10 (browser smoke) is deferred as E2E. All `[stretch]` tasks (T11 to T18) were skipped, as instructed.

| Task | Status | Tests added | Verification | Commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| T01, T02, T04 | Already ticked before this run | – | – | – |
| T03 one-query read model | [x] | 6 unit, 3 `pg_` | Clippy clean, workspace green | b36e8f3 |
| T05 `GET /api/dashboard` | [x] | 1 HTTP (401), 1 `pg_` (200 with all sections) | Gate green | 09e563d |
| T06 privacy and aggregates [SUPERVISED] | [x] | 5 `pg_` | Removing the owner filter makes the isolation test fail (temporary mutation, restored) | 58f7492 |
| T07 API contract and failure | [x] | 1 HTTP (503 with no SQL in the body), 1 `pg_` (exact keys, no code, active run has no verdict) | Gate green | a12004a |
| T08 core checkpoint [SUPERVISED] | [x] | – | fmt, clippy (0 findings), 1026 workspace tests, dashboard tests, `cargo deny` licences, `docker compose config`, web check and build all pass | 7c3210f |
| T09 core screen | [x] | 20 web (parser, labels, client, screen states) | `npm run check` 0 errors, 376 tests, build, ESLint clean on the new files | 2e6b112 |
| Review fixes (Wave 1 and 2) | Applied | 1 Rust (weak cap at 10), 5 parser rules, 1 screen (malformed response) | Workspace 1027 tests, 0 Clippy findings; web 382 tests | 084969d |
| T19 lantern art (optional) | [x] | 4 web (orange on loading and empty, poison only on an accepted newest run) | Web gate 386 tests, check, build | 5b621b9 |
| T10 core smoke path | Deferred: E2E (unchecked) | – | Needs browser sign-in, which Brighton ruled out | – |
| T11 to T18 `[stretch]` | Not started | – | – | – |

The web gate ran on the last commit with 386 tests passing. The full Rust gate ran before the final T19 commit, and that commit touched only web files.

### Blockers (in `docs/kiro-log/dashboard-fsrs-blockers.md`)

- **T10 is deferred as E2E**, per Brighton's rule against browser testing. The build emits `dashboard.html`, and the Rust HTTP tests cover the route.
- **Session-store failure returns 401, not 503 (review finding, Important, not fixed).** The shared `UserResolver` turns a database error into "not signed in". Fixing it changes a seam owned by the auth spec, so it needs Brighton's decision.
- **No catalogue list page in the web app.** The empty state has no "browse" link until that page exists.
- **Existing difficulty mismatch in `web/src/lib/api/types.ts`.** It uses `intro`, `standard` and `hard`, but the database uses `easy`, `medium` and `hard`. The problem page would reject real data. This is outside this spec, so I left it.
- **Impeccable launcher not run**, because Brighton's rule forbids downloading its engine. I followed its `SKILL.md` and `craft-floor.md` by hand.

### Review queue (in `docs/kiro-log/dashboard-fsrs-review-queue.md`)

- **T06** (`58f7492`): check `pg_dashboard_privacy.rs`. Canary checks read only the private sections, because public concept names and slugs legitimately appear in suggestions.
- **T08** (`7c3210f`): check the checkpoint evidence. T10 is still open.

### Open Minor review findings (not fixed)

- Frontend: the fetch runs in `$effect`, and a retry does not cancel an in-flight load. The components are in one file, not the `components/` folder that T09 names. Recent runs show raw `mode` values. There is no keyboard-focus test.
- Rust: `DashboardError::Internal` is never constructed. Decode failures carry no context string.[INFO] [KRS] <-- GenerateAssistantResponseCommand done totalEvents=359

